1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,965
Your graphics card has graphics in its name.

2
00:00:03,245 --> 00:00:08,493
But some of the most important work GPUs do today has nothing to do with games.

3
00:00:09,243 --> 00:00:12,959
A GPU is thousands of small cores working at once.

4
00:00:13,239 --> 00:00:20,713
That's perfect for drawing pixels, but it's perfect for any job that splits into lots of small, independent pieces.

5
00:00:21,463 --> 00:00:24,036
Artificial intelligence is the big one.

6
00:00:24,316 --> 00:00:33,657
Training and running AI models is mostly enormous piles of multiplication, and a GPU can do huge amounts of it in parallel.

7
00:00:34,407 --> 00:00:39,358
Scientists use GPUs to simulate weather, molecules and proteins.

8
00:00:39,638 --> 00:00:43,462
Video editors use them to speed up effects and exports.

9
00:00:44,212 --> 00:00:46,775
So a GPU isn't really a graphics chip.

10
00:00:47,055 --> 00:00:51,132
It's a parallel math machine that happens to be great at graphics.

11
00:00:51,412 --> 00:00:53,978
More PC hardware explained on the channel.

